# Level 1-06: Careful Steps — introduces Hazard. It sits in its own dead-end branch off
# the spine, away from the actual route, so the player can wander over and discover what
# it does entirely by choice. The real solution (a plain plate-hold like 1-01) never goes
# near it.
#
# Trace (spine at x=3, spawn (3,0), goal (3,9), door (3,8)=door:and:p1):
#   Branch to plate P: (3,5)-(2,5)-(1,5). Branch to hazard H (decoy, off the solution):
#   (3,2)-(4,2)-(5,2). Both are dead ends reachable straight off the spine.
#   Loop 1 (recorded): tick1 (3,1), tick2 (3,2) [passes the hazard junction without
#     turning into it], tick3 (3,3), tick4 (3,4), tick5 (3,5), tick6 (2,5), tick7 (1,5)=P.
#     Plate P activates at tick7 (occupancy-based, no Interact needed) and the AND door
#     recomputes open immediately. Loop then runs its full LOOP_SECONDS timer and spawns
#     a ghost that holds P for the rest of every future loop (idle-forever past its
#     recording).
#   Loop 2 (final, live, unencumbered): ghost1 replays the tick1-7 path and is back on P
#     by tick7 of this loop too, holding the door open well before the player arrives.
#     Live player walks straight up the spine: tick1 (3,1) ... tick8 (3,8)=door (already
#     open since tick7, no bump), tick9 (3,9)=goal. Level complete at tick9 of loop 2.
#     The hazard at (5,2) is reachable (spine (3,2)->(4,2)->(5,2)) for anyone curious
#     enough to detour into it, but the traced solution above never sets foot there.
#   Total: 2 loops, ~9 ticks in the solving loop.
NAME: 1-06 Careful Steps
WORLD: 1
LOOP_SECONDS: 20
MAX_TIMELINES: 1
PAR_LOOPS: 2
PAR_TICKS: 15
GRID:
###G###
###D###
###.###
###.###
#P..###
###.###
###.###
